      "rationale": "The linear model dropped NMSE from 1.0 to 0.097. After removing the linear x and v terms, the residual x-bin means are all small (~0.0006 to 0.0031) and no longer monotone (high-x bin is smallest at 0.0022), so no strong curvature signal remains in x. The v-bin means are also all small (max 0.0056 at the second bin), with no monotone pattern. However, the v-bin rmse jumps to 0.0325 in the highest-v bin versus ~0.012-0.019 elsewhere, and the highest-v bin residual mean is the largest v value, hinting at amplitude-dependent structure. For a harmonic oscillator acceleration a = -kx - cv, a quadratic x term is not physically motivated, but adding it costs one parameter and least squares can zero it. I add a mild x^2 term to test for residual curvature while keeping the linear structure intact. Expected gain is small since the residuals look mostly like unstructured noise around 0.02 rmse.",
